{"uid":"2a6fb8add1687b21","name":"test_dependent_repointing_covers_only_both_neither_and_no_failed_task_named","fullName":"tests.test_cure_pass#test_dependent_repointing_covers_only_both_neither_and_no_failed_task_named","historyId":"e7fc8d2ac2d6fd15597095680663080a","time":{"start":1791946001920,"stop":1791946001952,"duration":32},"description":"Consolidated (task 001, PRD requirement D, net-zero fast-tier\n    offset for this task's own new coverage, #206): folds four former\n    nodes into one, every assertion kept --\n    `test_a_dependent_naming_only_the_failed_task_is_repointed_to_the_\n    cure_task`, `test_a_dependent_naming_both_the_failed_task_and_\n    another_task_keeps_the_other`, `test_a_dependent_naming_neither_id_\n    is_left_untouched` and `test_evidence_naming_no_failed_task_leaves_\n    every_dependsOn_untouched` -- the first three shared one\n    `insert_cure_tasks` call's worth of setup (a single failed task named\n    once in one finding's evidence, three dependents each shaped\n    differently around it) and are now driven together in one call; the\n    fourth (a `pending`, not `failed`, task named in the evidence) is the\n    second phase, its own separate tasks table and call, exactly as\n    before.\n\n    #209 defect 7 adds a THIRD phase to the same subject: the id may sit in\n    the finding's own `clause` rather than its `evidence` and the repoint\n    still fires. Measured in `deck-phase3k`: the dead id `205` was named in\n    the clause while the evidence held only commit shas, so nothing\n    repointed and the operator hand-wrote two `steer task-update` calls.\n    Its second half pins the narrowing that widening needs: a `#NNN` in the\n    clause is an issue citation, never a task id, so it repoints nothing.\n    Phases one and two are unchanged and neither of their clauses names any\n    task id -- both cite an issue as `(#149)`, which is exactly the shape\n    that must not match -- so both still prove exactly what they proved\n    before.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Consolidated (task 001, PRD requirement D, net-zero fast-tier<br />\noffset for this task's own new coverage, #206): folds four former<br />\nnodes into one, every assertion kept --<br />\n<code>test_a_dependent_naming_only_the_failed_task_is_repointed_to_the_ cure_task</code>, <code>test_a_dependent_naming_both_the_failed_task_and_ another_task_keeps_the_other</code>, <code>test_a_dependent_naming_neither_id_ is_left_untouched</code> and <code>test_evidence_naming_no_failed_task_leaves_ every_dependsOn_untouched</code> -- the first three shared one<br />\n<code>insert_cure_tasks</code> call's worth of setup (a single failed task named<br />\nonce in one finding's evidence, three dependents each shaped<br />\ndifferently around it) and are now driven together in one call; the<br />\nfourth (a <code>pending</code>, not <code>failed</code>, task named in the evidence) is the<br />\nsecond phase, its own separate tasks table and call, exactly as<br />\nbefore.</p>\n<pre><code>#209 defect 7 adds a THIRD phase to the same subject: the id may sit in\nthe finding's own `clause` rather than its `evidence` and the repoint\nstill fires. Measured in `deck-phase3k`: the dead id `205` was named in\nthe clause while the evidence held only commit shas, so nothing\nrepointed and the operator hand-wrote two `steer task-update` calls.\nIts second half pins the narrowing that widening needs: a `#NNN` in the\nclause is an issue citation, never a task id, so it repoints nothing.\nPhases one and two are unchanged and neither of their clauses names any\ntask id -- both cite an issue as `(#149)`, which is exactly the shape\nthat must not match -- so both still prove exactly what they proved\nbefore.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791945777623,"stop":1791945777623,"duration":0}